{
	title: 'Colour themes as plugins, switched by /theme',
	spec: "Themes are plugins (task an). Each theme is a tracked file themes/<name>.ts at the repo root (outside plugins/, so the loader does not load them all), written like any plugin: it overrides fields of colors (src/common/colors.ts, every field a function) with plugin.around, so removing it puts the built-in look back exactly. The active theme is plugins/color-theme.ts in the Hal home: a symlink to themes/<name>.ts, so a pull that improves a theme reaches the active one; plugins/.gitignore keeps it local. No link means the built-in palette in colors.ts, called default (there is no themes/default.ts). Shipped themes: phosphor (today's hues louder on near-black), nostromo (Alien: amber text, green phosphor), hal (2001: black, white, HAL red, errors magenta), all following the look in tasks/README.md (no slate, no glow). A theme repaints what it can in plugin.onChange: open terminals redraw; the web page picks the theme up on its next load (its colour CSS is generated per page load). /theme (host command) with no argument lists default and every themes/*.ts, marking the active one; /theme <name> points the link at it (default removes the link); an unknown name is an error listing the choices. Later (not this task): pages repaint live when the theme changes; the first-run questions offer a theme and switch it live as the answer changes.",
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['an']
}
